  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "Loss and detection controls in the three-spin Rabi chain. {(a):} Endpoint concurrence $\\mathcal C_{13}$ for uniformly low number losses $(0.04,0.04,0.04)\\omega_c$, with feedback off (grey) and on (purple). {(b):} The same feedback-off/on comparison for weak-end losses $(0.04,0.52,0.04)\\omega_c$, with feedback on in orange. These panels isolate the effect of feedback within each loss profile. {(c):} Feedback-on curves only: uniformly low loss (purple), weak ends (orange), and weak ends with reduced detection efficiency $\\eta=0.04/0.52$ (teal). The purple and orange curves repeat the feedback-on results of {(a,b)}; the feedback-off baselines are absent. Detection is ideal except for the teal control. {(d):} Spin--detected-quadrature covariance $\\sqrt{\\eta\\kappa_2}\\,\\mathrm{Cov}(S_1^y,\\sqrt{2}p_2)$ for the same three feedback-on cases and colours as {(c)}, with $p_2=(a_2-a_2^\\dagger)/(i\\sqrt{2})$. This diagnostic is not an information rate. {The plots in} {(a--c)} share a vertical scale. Solid cap-six and dotted cap-five master-equation curves test the photon cutoff; the largest relevant all-low cap change is about $1.5\\times10^{-3}$. These deterministic mechanism controls are not HOPS and have no Monte Carlo uncertainty."
